{"dependencies":["Finset.instSetLike","Finset.partialOrder","Finset.mk","SetLike.coe","Finset","Finset.val","Finset.disjiUnion._proof_1","Set.PairwiseDisjoint","Function.comp","Multiset","Finset.instOrderBot","Multiset.bind"],"doc":"`disjiUnion s f h` is the set such that `a ∈ disjiUnion s f` iff `a ∈ f i` for some `i ∈ s`.\nIt is the same as `s.biUnion f`, but it does not require decidable equality on the type. The\nhypothesis ensures that the sets are disjoint. ","extra":null,"kind":"definition","levels":["u_1","u_2"],"module":"Mathlib.Data.Finset.Union","name":"Finset.disjiUnion","nodes":[["sort",["succ",["param","u_1"]]],["sort",["succ",["param","u_2"]]],["constant","Finset",[["param","u_1"]]],["bound",1],["apply",2,3],["bound",2],["constant","Finset",[["param","u_2"]]],["apply",6,5],["forall","a._@._internal._hyg.0",5,7,"explicit"],["constant","Set.PairwiseDisjoint",[["param","u_2"],["param","u_1"]]],["apply",9,7],["bound",3],["apply",10,11],["constant","Finset.partialOrder",[["param","u_2"]]],["apply",13,5],["apply",12,14],["constant","Finset.instOrderBot",[["param","u_2"]]],["apply",16,5],["apply",15,17],["constant","SetLike.coe",[["param","u_1"],["param","u_1"]]],["apply",2,11],["apply",19,20],["apply",21,11],["constant","Finset.instSetLike",[["param","u_1"]]],["apply",23,11],["apply",22,24],["apply",25,3],["apply",18,26],["bound",0],["apply",27,28],["apply",6,11],["forall","hf",29,30,"explicit"],["forall","t",8,31,"explicit"],["forall","s",4,32,"explicit"],["forall","β",1,33,"implicit"],["forall","α",0,34,"implicit"],["constant","Finset.mk",[["param","u_2"]]],["apply",36,11],["constant","Multiset.bind",[["param","u_2"],["param","u_1"]]],["bound",4],["apply",38,39],["apply",40,11],["constant","Finset.val",[["param","u_1"]]],["apply",42,39],["apply",43,5],["apply",41,44],["constant","Function.comp",[["succ",["param","u_1"]],["succ",["param","u_2"]],["succ",["param","u_2"]]]],["apply",46,39],["apply",47,30],["constant","Multiset",[["param","u_2"]]],["apply",49,11],["apply",48,50],["constant","Finset.val",[["param","u_2"]]],["apply",52,11],["apply",51,53],["apply",54,3],["apply",45,55],["apply",37,56],["constant","Finset.disjiUnion._proof_1",[["param","u_2"],["param","u_1"]]],["apply",58,39],["apply",59,11],["apply",60,5],["apply",61,3],["apply",62,28],["apply",57,63],["lambda","hf",29,64,"explicit"],["lambda","t",8,65,"explicit"],["lambda","s",4,66,"explicit"],["lambda","β",1,67,"implicit"],["lambda","α",0,68,"implicit"]],"project":false,"range":{"column":0,"endColumn":97,"endLine":45,"line":40},"type":35,"typeText":"{α : Type u_1} →\n  {β : Type u_2} →\n    (s : Finset.{u_1} α) → (t : α → Finset.{u_2} β) → Set.PairwiseDisjoint.{u_2, u_1} (↑s) t → Finset.{u_2} β","unsafe":false,"value":69,"source":{"code":"/-- `disjiUnion s f h` is the set such that `a ∈ disjiUnion s f` iff `a ∈ f i` for some `i ∈ s`.\nIt is the same as `s.biUnion f`, but it does not require decidable equality on the type. The\nhypothesis ensures that the sets are disjoint. -/\ndef disjiUnion (s : Finset α) (t : α → Finset β) (hf : (s : Set α).PairwiseDisjoint t) : Finset β :=\n  ⟨s.val.bind (Finset.val ∘ t), Multiset.nodup_bind.2\n    ⟨fun a _ ↦ (t a).nodup, s.nodup.pairwise fun _ ha _ hb hab ↦ disjoint_val.2 <| hf ha hb hab⟩⟩","start":40,"end":45},"axioms":["Classical.choice","Quot.sound","propext"]}